<speak>That is a less demanding way to share them. Everyone can look at their own pace, and the conversation does not get interrupted by a long sequence of attachments. You seem to favour arrangements that make things easier to find without making them overly elaborate. A small album, a plainly labelled folder, a short office guide. They each have a clear purpose. Outside travelling, what is your favourite way to have a quiet afternoon when there is nothing scheduled?</speak>